# Payment Security — CRITICAL

- Never trust client-side price, total, discount, shipping, currency, or payment status.
- Recalculate authoritative totals server-side.
- Never let the browser mark an order as paid.
- Verify gateway callbacks/webhooks server-side.
- Verify signatures when supported.
- Verify order ID, transaction ID, amount, currency, and expected event.
- Make webhook/payment processing idempotent.
- Prevent duplicate orders, charges, refunds, and stock deductions.
- Keep gateway secrets server-side.
- Never expose private gateway credentials to the browser.
- Never log raw card data, CVV, secrets, or authentication tokens.
- Prefer provider-hosted/tokenized payment flows so the application does not handle raw card data unnecessarily.
- Refunds require server-side authorization and controlled gateway operations.
- Maintain auditable payment state transitions.
- Add tests for invalid signatures, duplicate events, amount mismatch, invalid transaction, and unauthorized access.
- Read `docs/PAYMENT_SECURITY.md` before implementing payment features.
